# The reviewed target-selection policy for the opengrep packs (P3.1, A-10).
#
# Deliberately EMPTY of patterns. The recipe passes this file via --semgrepignore-filename, which
# replaces both the tool's built-in default ignore (which silently skipped whole source trees such
# as tests/) and any .semgrepignore the audited target ships. A target-controlled ignore file must
# not be able to shrink the reviewed scan scope; the recipe still inventories its presence and
# records it on the result.
#
# Reviewed scope is therefore: every file matching the packs' languages under the application
# root, minus the recipe's reviewed directory exclusions. Declaration files (*.d.ts) carry no
# runtime behaviour, are not inventoried, and are not scanned by the tool; secret material in any
# file is covered by the gitleaks recipes regardless of extension.
